learnings:
  - 'Anti-spoof is enforced at the auth layer: JWT audience (user vs agent). Human /checkout rejects agent grants; /agent/checkout rejects user tokens. An agent can''t take the ungated human path.'
  - 'PAYMENTS_MODE=mock (default) lets the whole flow (human + agent) complete with no Circle creds; the real Circle transfer is the same #payment-service seam under PAYMENTS_MODE=circle.'
  - Verification sessions are single-use via an atomic UPDATE ... where status='pending' ... RETURNING, so a double-clicked verify link settles the order exactly once.
  - Express 4 does not forward async throws to error middleware; added an asyncHandler wrapper applied to every async route + a central error handler, fixing the prior /checkout hang.
  - Background Bash tasks in this environment launch with cwd = the client dir; long-running server/vite processes must cd explicitly. TaskStop leaves the OS process alive (orphaned child keeps serving) — use PowerShell Stop-Process by port owner to truly kill.
  - The prompt-logging UserPromptSubmit hook stopped recording after 'yes lets please continue'; backfilled this session's prompts manually into prompts/matt.jsonl. Root-cause the hook (.claude/hooks/log-prompt.sh) later.
